[COMMENTS]
STATION,Velocity area station with small truncated Flat V weir gauging a relatively flat, rural catchment. GENERAL: Velocity area station with small truncated Flat V weir approx 4.3m wide, low wingwalls in straight channel. Located approximately 150m downstream of a road bridge in open pasture. STATION HYDROMETRY: The weir was primarily constructed as a low flow gauge and drowns out at a relatively low level. Large flows spill onto the right bank floodplain. Rating developed from gaugings, with modelled top-end to allow for bypassing / out of bank flow. FLOW RECORD: Early daily flows held for Apr 1972-Jan 1975. Daily and peak flows held from Sept 1984. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2023 (WINFAP Files v12). FLOW REGIME: Predominantly natural flow regime. Minor impact from groundwater abstractions.
CATCHMENT,Relatively flat, mainly agricultural rural area, with sandstones in lower part and mudstones in upper catchment.
Qmed Suitability,Rating well supported by gaugings to QMED.
Pooling Suitability,Too much uncertainty once flows are out-of-bank.
[END]
